# Git push — studentsabroad

When the user says **git push**, **push**, or asks to push changes:

- **Repository:** https://github.com/glasz-cloud/studentsabroad.git
- **Remote:** `origin`
- **Branch:** `main` (always push here unless they specify another branch)

## Workflow

1. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log -3` to see state.
2. If there are uncommitted changes the user clearly wants pushed, stage and commit first (only when push implies shipping current work).
3. Ensure remote is set: `git remote get-url origin` → should be `https://github.com/glasz-cloud/studentsabroad.git`. If missing: `git remote add origin https://github.com/glasz-cloud/studentsabroad.git`. If wrong: `git remote set-url origin https://github.com/glasz-cloud/studentsabroad.git`.
4. Push: `git push -u origin main` (or `git push` once upstream is configured).
5. Do **not** ask the user to paste the repo URL again — use the URL above.

Do not update global git config (user.name, user.email). Do not force-push to main unless explicitly requested.
